prompt:
Create one original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA spritesheet for Moxie Capwell of Moonmorel Hex performing a right-facing jump block. Match the canon portrait and gameplay references. She is an adult human woman with pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, long thick lavender hair in a high ponytail with a small gold hair tie, mature athletic build, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-tops. Preserve her face, eyes, ponytail, tie, kit and ordinary human anatomy. No witch hat, beard, male, monster, robot, new character, or costume.

Draw clean readable late-1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel art. Exactly four full-body poses in a 2-column by 2-row grid, row-major, with broad transparent gutters and margin. Every hair strand, hand and shoe remains inside its cell. Poses are distinct and connected; two arms/two legs only. Hands are empty; the ball belongs to a separate game object and is never drawn. No ball, sphere, hoop, rim, court, floor, shadows, effects, text, border, teammates or scenery.

0 defensive stance, facing right, knees flexed and both hands low;
1 plant and jump, lead arm rising while the other arm balances;
2 peak block at simulation tick4: both arms stretch straight upward, fingers wide and empty, full body airborne;
3 descend and land with knees flexed, arms lowering.

Keep the high ponytail/gold tie unobscured and separated from the raised hands. Preserve the same Moxie face, eyes, clothing palette, adult proportions and shoes. Return only a true-transparent RGBA sheet with no alpha haze, checkerboard, matte, speckles or colored halo.
